// The night sky's data: the 5044 stars visible to the naked eye (to magnitude 6) and the outline of the Milky Way.
// From d3-celestial (https://github.com/ofrohn/d3-celestial), whose star data comes from the HYG database
// (Hipparcos, Yale Bright Star and Gliese catalogues) and Milky Way outline from Jose R. Vieira.
//
// STARS: base64 of 8 bytes a star, little-endian uint16 x4: right ascension (0..65535 = 0..360 degrees),
// declination (0..65535 = -90..+90), (magnitude + 2) * 1000, (colour index B-V + 0.5) * 20000.
// MILKY_WAY: a 512 x 256 PNG in right ascension (across, 0 to 360 degrees) and declination (down, +90 to -90),
// its five levels of brightness filled and softened (a wide blur under a fine one, so its edges fade as the real
// one's do).
